    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 2914: Minimum Number of Changes to Make Binary String Beautiful (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given a 0-indexed binary string s having an even length. A string is beautiful if
                it is possible to partition it into one or more substrings such that each substring has an
                even length and contains only 1's or only 0's. You can change any character in s to 0 or 1.
                Return the minimum number of changes required to make the string s beautiful.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: s = "1001"<br>
                Output: 2<br>
                Explanation: We change s[1] to 1 and s[3] to 0 to obtain the string "1100". It can be
                partitioned into "11" and "00", each of even length and with identical characters. It can be
                seen that the string cannot be made beautiful with fewer than 2 changes.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int minChanges(string s) {
        int cnt = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; s.length(); i += 2) {
            if (s[i] != s[i + 1]) {
                cnt++;
            }
        }
        return cnt;
    }
};</code></pre>
